The convention in this repository is to have one TEST or TEST_F for each method/function you are testing.

Sometimes the method is not public, so it has to be tested indirectly by calling public methods.

But please organize your tests so that each TEST or TEST_F covers all the variations for a single method/function.

You can put blocks of code around each variation so that you don't run into duplicate local variables.

e.g.
```
TEST_F(ManagerTests, Method_Being_Tested)
{
    // Test where file is found
    {
       ...
    }

    // Test where file is not found
    {
       ...
    }
}
```
